# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# One Interiors — environment
#
# v0.1 runs entirely on fixture data and needs NONE of these.
# Deploy to Vercel with an empty environment and it will work.
# Fill these in as each subsystem is wired up (see README).
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# ── Supabase project ──
# The publishable key is PUBLIC by design — it ships in the browser bundle.
# It is safe only because Row Level Security decides what it can reach. With
# RLS off, this key is full read/write on every table. See docs/DATABASE.md.
# Nothing uses these yet; they are here for Storage (evidence uploads, OI-5c).
SUPABASE_URL=""
SUPABASE_PUBLISHABLE_KEY=""
NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL=""
NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_PUBLISHABLE_KEY=""

# Public endpoint. Used to verify Supabase-issued JWTs if we ever accept them.
SUPABASE_JWKS_URL=""

# ── The secret key ──
# sb_secret_ (and the legacy service_role key) BYPASS Row Level Security
# entirely: full read/write on every table, all storage, admin operations.
#
#   · Server-only. NEVER prefix it with NEXT_PUBLIC_ — that inlines it into the
#     browser bundle and publishes it to every visitor.
#   · Never commit it, never send it through chat, Slack or email.
#   · If it is ever exposed, rotate it in Supabase → Settings → API Keys.
#     Rotation is cheap; a leaked key with RLS bypass is not.
#
# Prisma does NOT need it — it authenticates with the database password. One
# feature does: floor-plan upload (src/modules/storage/floor-plan.ts). Supabase
# Storage authorises with either a Supabase-issued user JWT or this key, and our
# sessions are our own, in Postgres — so a server-side upload has to present it.
# Exactly one module reads it, and with it blank, upload is simply off and the
# prep pack asks for the carpet area alone.
#
# Requires a PRIVATE bucket named `floor-plans` in the Supabase project. A
# public bucket here would put the layout of somebody's home, usually with the
# flat number on it, behind a guessable permanent URL.
SUPABASE_SECRET_KEY=""

# ── Database — Supabase (see docs/DATABASE.md) ──
# BOTH are required. Pooled for runtime, direct for migrations; migrations
# through the pooler hang. Leave blank to run on fixture studios.
DATABASE_URL=""   # transaction pooler, port 6543, ?pgbouncer=true
DIRECT_URL=""     # direct connection, port 5432
REDIS_URL=""

# ── Sessions ──
# openssl rand -base64 32 — generate a DIFFERENT one for production.
SESSION_SECRET=""

# ── WhatsApp Business API — OTP login + milestone notifications ──
# Meta business verification has a lead time. Start it early.
WHATSAPP_PHONE_NUMBER_ID=""
WHATSAPP_ACCESS_TOKEN=""
WHATSAPP_WEBHOOK_VERIFY_TOKEN=""
# The approved template that carries the sign-in code. Must be category
# AUTHENTICATION — a free-form message to someone who has not written to you in
# the last 24 hours is rejected, which is every first-time customer.
# Configurable so an approval delay does not need a code change.
WHATSAPP_OTP_TEMPLATE="one_interiors_otp"
WHATSAPP_OTP_LOCALE="en"

# ── Pre-launch scaffolding — DELETE BOTH BEFORE THE FIRST REAL CUSTOMER ──
# Each refuses to work once NEXT_PUBLIC_ROSTER_IS_REAL=1, so declaring the
# roster real disables them everywhere at once.
#
# Show studios that have not passed verification, so the funnel can be walked
# before any studio is live.
DEV_SHOW_UNVERIFIED_STUDIOS=""
# Print the sign-in code on the page instead of waiting for WhatsApp.
# WARNING: with this on the OTP verifies NOTHING — anyone can claim any number.
# It exists only so the pages behind the sign-in gate are testable while a
# WhatsApp template waits on Meta approval.
DEV_SHOW_OTP_ON_SCREEN=""
# Open /ops to anyone with the URL.
# WARNING: the widest of these three. Exposes every studio's legal name and
# GSTIN, our private assessment of each, and consultation requests carrying a
# name, phone number and email. Acceptable only while every studio is a
# placeholder.
DEV_OPS_NO_AUTH=""

# ── Escrow provider (sprint 6) ──
# RBI rules: a licensed partner holds client funds, never us.
ESCROW_PROVIDER="sandbox"
ESCROW_API_KEY=""
ESCROW_WEBHOOK_SECRET=""

# ── Subscription billing (phase 2) ──
RAZORPAY_KEY_ID=""
RAZORPAY_KEY_SECRET=""
RAZORPAY_WEBHOOK_SECRET=""

# ── KYC / registry lookups (sprint 3) ──
# idfy | signzy | surepass | authbridge — none publish flat pricing, get quotes
KYC_PROVIDER=""
KYC_API_KEY=""

# ── Object storage — milestone photos, verification evidence ──
# Private by default. Never serve these from a public bucket.
S3_ENDPOINT=""
S3_BUCKET=""
S3_ACCESS_KEY_ID=""
S3_SECRET_ACCESS_KEY=""

# ── Analytics ──
NEXT_PUBLIC_POSTHOG_KEY=""
NEXT_PUBLIC_POSTHOG_HOST="https://app.posthog.com"

# ── Public config ──
# Set to "1" ONLY once the roster is real pilot studios rather than the
# invented fixtures. Anything else (including unset) shows the pre-launch
# notice on every page. Default errs toward disclosure on purpose.
NEXT_PUBLIC_ROSTER_IS_REAL=""

NEXT_PUBLIC_SITE_URL="http://localhost:3000"

# ── Portfolio drafting agent ─────────────────────────────────────
# Optional. With this unset, drafting is simply off and studios write
# their own copy — nothing else changes, and every test runs without it.
#
# The agent only ever sees facts from our own database, and every draft
# is machine-checked against those facts before a human sees it: any
# number it cannot trace fails the draft. See
# src/modules/studio/portfolio-draft.ts.
ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=""
# Optional override. Defaults to claude-sonnet-5.
ANTHROPIC_MODEL=""

# ── Which hostname serves which product ──────────────────────────────
#
# Set all three together, or none. With none set, one origin serves
# everything by path, exactly as it did before — which is how local
# development and every Vercel preview deployment run.
#
# Sessions are host-only (no cookie `domain`), so splitting the hosts
# splits the sessions: an ops cookie is never sent to the studio host.
# That also means a magic link MUST point at the host it will be
# redeemed on — see `siteUrlFor` in src/lib/site.ts.
STUDIO_HOST=studio.oneinteriors.in
OPS_HOST=ops.oneinteriors.in
PUBLIC_HOST=oneinteriors.in

# The customer marketplace. Unset means /quiz, /match, /compare,
# /expert, /prepare, /account, /studios and /verification are not
# served — the apex is the waitlist, which is its own Vercel project.
# Set to 1 on the day the marketplace opens.
CUSTOMER_LIVE=

# ── Outbound email (Resend) ──────────────────────────────────────────
#
# Both, or neither. With neither set, sign-in links print to the dev
# server console instead of sending — which is how the app runs offline.
# In production a missing provider is a hard failure rather than a
# silent one, because "the email quietly never sent" is the worst
# outcome. See src/modules/auth/email.ts.
RESEND_API_KEY=

# ⚠️ The single most common way to get this wrong.
#
# EMAIL_FROM must use a domain you have VERIFIED in Resend. Resend's
# shared sandbox sender, `onboarding@resend.dev`, looks like it works
# and does not: it delivers ONLY to the address that owns the Resend
# account and returns 403 for every other recipient. Verifying your
# domain does nothing by itself — this line has to use it.
#
# Symptom when it is wrong: the app reports the email as not delivered
# and the server log carries the provider's own words, e.g.
#   [auth] Resend 403: You can only send testing emails to your own
#   email address
#
# The mailbox does not need to exist to SEND. It does need to exist to
# RECEIVE: the studio welcome email invites a reply and promises a
# person reads it.
EMAIL_FROM=One Interiors <hello@oneinteriors.in>

# Shared secret for POST /api/waitlist, set to the SAME value in the
# oneinteriors.in waitlist project. Generate one with:
#   node -e "console.log(require('crypto').randomBytes(32).toString('base64url'))"
# Unset means the route refuses everything, which is the safe default.
WAITLIST_INGEST_TOKEN=
